{
  "dom_id": "step-q69157",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "$\\sqrt[4]{{3}^{5}}=$",
  "worked_solution": "The radical $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ can be written using a fractional exponent as ${x}^{1/n}.$\n\nComparing $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ with $\\sqrt[4]{{3}^{5}},$ we get $x={3}^{5}$ and $n=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4]{{3}^{5}}={({3}^{5})}^{1/4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the power law for exponents, we have\n\n$$\n{({3}^{5})}^{1/4}={3}^{5/4}.\n$$",
